    "homeType": "MULTI_FAMILY",
    "description": "This trophy investment asset is situated at the corner of Haight Street and Central Avenue, near the lush Buena Vista Park surrounded by well-preserved and modernized Victorian-era buildings. The desirable 12-unit mixed-use property features 8 full-floor, 4-room flats with individual entries, atop 4 thriving neighborhood-serving retail stores. The building is nicely painted, well-maintained, and spans 13,225 square feet. It has undergone numerous improvements, including a significant electrical power upgrade in recent years. 4 out of 8 residential units have been modernized while retaining their ornate decorative motifs and period details. A newly vacated unit is available for a new owner to upgrade, occupy, or rent out. Built in 1910 and zoned NCD (Haight Street Neighborhood Commercial District), this charming low-rise garden-style property is within walking distance of the popular Panhandle Park area, ideal for recreation and relaxation. Located on a quiet section of the world-renowned Haight Street, it offers a multitude of eclectic shopping options and a nostalgic glimpse into the hippie era.  This rarely available property is perfect for investors seeking a distinctive and well-situated asset in the heart of San Francisco."
  },
